# Introduction

Carve keeps the authoring source readable while `carve-latex` owns publication typography
[@carve2026], which a second cite states integrally as [+@carve2026].

## A theorem

::: theorem
Every supported structural node is translated from the canonical AST rather than reparsed from HTML.
:::

::: note "On the fidelity report"
Every unsupported construct is classified rather than dropped in silence.
:::

::: warning
A warning prints its own label, not "Remark".
:::

::: tip
Each notice kind has its own environment.
:::

::: danger
So does this one.
:::

::: info
And this one.
:::

::: success
And this one.
:::

::: example
And this one.
:::

::: quote
And this one.
:::

